course: dictionary
lesson: 13727
title: Integral: a necessary part of a whole
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how important one thing is to a whole. Read the words around the word to find its meaning. «Wheels are an integral part of a bike, and you cannot ride without them.» You cannot ride without wheels, so integral means necessary and important.
explain: Integral can also mean built in, made as one piece with something. «The mug's handle is integral, made in one piece with the cup.» The clue is made in one piece: the handle is not stuck on afterwards. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Integral is different from integer. An integer is a whole number, such as 7. Integral is a different word, although the two are related. In advanced maths, an integral is a calculation that finds things like the area under a curve.
fact: Integral means necessary and important as a part of a whole.
fact: «Integral» can also mean built in, made as one piece with something.
fact: «An integral part of the team» means a key member of the team.
fact: In advanced maths, an integral is a calculation in calculus that finds things like the area under a curve.
fact: «Integer» means a whole number. It is a different word, but related to integral.
exercise: «Wheels are an integral part of a bike, and you cannot ride without them.» What does integral mean here? | Very heavy | *Necessary, a key part of the whole | Decorative, added just for looks | Painted in bright colours
exercise: «The mug's handle is integral, made in one piece with the cup.» What does integral mean here? | Broken | *Built in, made as one piece with the cup | Stuck on afterwards | Cold to touch
exercise: Ella says integral is just another word for integer. What is the right answer? | They mean exactly the same | *An integer is a whole number, and integral is a different but related word | An integral is a whole number
test: «Good sleep is an integral part of staying well.» What does integral suggest? | Very noisy | *Necessary and important, a key part | Not needed at all | Only needed at weekends
test: In advanced maths, what does an integral find? | A type of bike | The colour of a graph | The number of whole numbers | *The area under a curve
exam: «The bass is an integral part of the song.» What does integral mean here? | *Necessary, a key part of the whole | Quiet and small | Old and broken | Something you can throw away
